From 4355c071e7960c7c305dc356a84e919c80bb89f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xuxh1 <18172956238@163.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 21:01:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sites): tower wetland vegetated fraction
 DEF_WETLAND_FVEG_SITE

New single-point key DEF_WETLAND_FVEG_SITE (real, default -1 = off): the
measured vascular cover of a tower footprint becomes fveg of the wetland
patch (patchtype 2) in LAI_readin; 0 removes the canopy (tlai, tsai and
green set to 0).

CoLM202X no longer reads fveg in the canopy physics (sigf is the
snow-free fraction from snowfraction and the canopy covers the whole
patch), so the fraction is consumed where the wetland canopy is solved:
- albland: two-stream at lai/fveg and sai/fveg; albedo, sunlit and
  shaded absorption and transmittance averaged with the open ground, as
  twostream_wrap averages a bare PFT.
- THERMAL: LeafTemperature per unit canopy area (lai, sai, absorbed
  solar and PAR, foliage water and interception divided by fveg); canopy
  fluxes, assimilation, respiration and foliage water times fveg; ground
  and turbulent fluxes averaged with the bare-ground GroundFluxes values;
  raw_grnd from the two conductances in parallel. Leaf temperature, water
  potential, stomatal and ozone state and z0m stay those of the canopy.
tlai and tsai stay patch means, as the methane module, the wetland LAI
cap and interception read them.

With the key off a wetland patch keeps fveg = fveg0 = 1, the new
branches are not entered and THERMAL passes exact copies of its inputs
to LeafTemperature, so results are unchanged.

